{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-product-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0323","math_ordinal":40,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The product is indexed by i over J, so its factor must be alpha_i; alpha_j leaves j free and does not describe the stated family product.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:93","source_normalized_sha256":"a888a581b2b97ce2659dc48304ee24096809e10dabb40bde90ab7ea28c5a5b11","source_text":"\\prod_{i\\in J}\\alpha_j","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:91","target_normalized_sha256":"155ea9abce52b187b1de04e8ae03a2a6af2eea5414753b17f7443310b7b95cda","target_text":"\\prod_{i\\in J}\\alpha_i","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-product-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0324","math_ordinal":134,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The preceding factors and intersection are indexed by j; the printed product binds i while leaving j free.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:232","source_normalized_sha256":"2dc9113e4f42ef9ffa47f62a0e67c3d3bbaea48ca93a1aa2fe58b235632dff85","source_text":"\\prod_{i=1}^n\\hat\\mu E_j","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:233","target_normalized_sha256":"9127c6e7b948e3e71f832d7d5fdd722a37c889e6c7c5d162101c7777ef2ea8c9","target_text":"\\prod_{j=1}^n\\hat\\mu E_j","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-terminal-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0325","math_ordinal":135,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proof fixed E_1 through E_n and no k is bound in this implication; the arbitrariness claim must refer to those n sets.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:234","source_normalized_sha256":"6214945561b2be7967b5d80ebe12f121ca4073399c5aa9ab5b550af1d9ebb45e","source_text":"E_1,\\ldots,E_k","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:235","target_normalized_sha256":"81b910fd8e91f49d9b5244eb1ee7549121c739a6e80476f6273850b0ef0b018c","target_text":"E_1,\\ldots,E_n","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-product-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0326","math_ordinal":145,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The factor is parameterized by j through both i_j and F_j; binding i leaves j free.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:247","source_normalized_sha256":"f068f8236c79a742364b4f524c921e9c6aa0aaf38d4c1504253e31968953dd03","source_text":"\\prod_{i=1}^n\\hat\\mu X_{i_j}^{-1}[F_j]","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:248","target_normalized_sha256":"0fdbc51384c718b1a9cdfff04a1093c7f1d147f8beae01369a601c0913d995cd","target_text":"\\prod_{j=1}^n\\hat\\mu X_{i_j}^{-1}[F_j]","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-family-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0327","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proposition declares the family h_i, so the generated sigma-algebra and measurability argument must use h_i(X_i), not an unbound common h. Both occurrences carry the same repair.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:265","source_normalized_sha256":"667418c09e021ade727c8df3770ccd25640a82305584e114e2004ff74b01bc19","source_text":"h(X_i)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:267","target_normalized_sha256":"7cd264d11c04f8a4f0eeb8b5dfbc14b4f8e4c0fa940cf6245f9c7428ec2627b8","target_text":"h_i(X_i)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-set-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0328","math_ordinal":281,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proof declared E_j in Sigma_{i_j}; E_{i_j} is not declared and must be E_j in the diagonal-preimage identity.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:446","source_normalized_sha256":"25258e7e0f448c315ae8faf0ca2e13b6812e9cc0880500e2a90ac2cdc33f443b","source_text":"\\bigcap_{j\\le n}E_{i_j}","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:450","target_normalized_sha256":"1957ece3c149f9e7829530b56583322b4237ba3515a042d31e88a510c4784fa1","target_text":"\\bigcap_{j\\le n}E_j","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-set-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0329","math_ordinal":283,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The same declared events E_j must appear in the measure-product computation; E_{i_j} is undefined in this proof.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:449-452","source_normalized_sha256":"0901e0b7386bfb45b435ac23499b59f52636fe39c35943ddb34100e141d4767f","source_text":"\\mu_{i_j}E_{i_j}","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:453-456","target_normalized_sha256":"971a33fae30ac4a611ad589889a357d2c3f0e9ec10618a484da6057e84fff7c4","target_text":"\\mu_{i_j}E_j","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-underlying-space-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0330","math_ordinal":406,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"In the product-space cylinder argument E_i must equal the full factor space Omega_i outside finite J; X_i denotes a random variable and cannot serve as the factor set.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:597","source_normalized_sha256":"ef9e9525c666219486d0f0d70229be27bfc3df987cf64868cb48156fade11764","source_text":"E_i=X_i","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:600","target_normalized_sha256":"421eb9aa2e5a65e4eee57df5bcb20da76b4543e41695c29fd439bac4bdcb4101","target_text":"E_i=\\Omega_i","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-event-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0331","math_ordinal":421,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"F_{ij} are the declared Borel target sets; E_i is the product-coordinate event and E_{ij} is nowhere defined.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:620","source_normalized_sha256":"5e6a3afdefe43a50e1212327a13ec00587e98ff71c63911c4503165c73c566a0","source_text":"\\Pr(X_{ij}\\in E_{ij})","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:625","target_normalized_sha256":"d62b757d796d0b83f985b7acc0cedb67a8bec6e7274ce4f401d08337b188fc62","target_text":"\\Pr(X_{ij}\\in F_{ij})","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-product-space-type-and-index-errors","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0332","math_ordinal":453,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The H_i are coordinate subsets whose product lies in the product space; J is undefined, and membership in Sigma_i concerns each coordinate map phi_i. The printed intersection and unindexed preimage are ill-typed.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:669-675","source_normalized_sha256":"7a02b7f71d04b1d82bc007811b3b207b5a9986771c9893c02483a69a22e042d2","source_text":"\\mu\\phi^{-1}[\\bigcap_{i\\in I}H_i]","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:675-681","target_normalized_sha256":"ada0896dc2a33800b001ecd5348f9e260f36727bd3cea50553ce02f3d1687a4e","target_text":"\\mu\\phi^{-1}[\\prod_{i\\in I}H_i]","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-event-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0333","math_ordinal":512,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proof defined the tail event E_a and immediately uses its measure; bare E is not defined in this argument.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:771","source_normalized_sha256":"527eb9752aa28e47fe0a25244d78d918968381f828d52d8ddcd7beb3bd254fa3","source_text":"E\\in\\Sigma_{\\infty}^*","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:777","target_normalized_sha256":"937cd0da1b33230663e5d2cf7468851aa382a7fe8d12a26bcfe7074a4e715c62","target_text":"E_a\\in\\Sigma_{\\infty}^*","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-terminal-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0334","math_ordinal":534,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The theorem quantifies E_r for r up to n and its displayed product also runs to n; j_r leaves the family length inconsistent.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:804","source_normalized_sha256":"6251c033ee2bb73a9591209a23e5b91d87f44de5fb6a3b741ff43783a39f947f","source_text":"j_1,\\ldots,j_r","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:811","target_normalized_sha256":"7af7ae41c45c803f2f0dc416dd876eb1c01539bfe378bcbc3e70a204e0fcf7a2","target_text":"j_1,\\ldots,j_n","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-terminal-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0335","math_ordinal":580,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proof repeats the theorem's n-member family and uses r only as the running index; the terminal subscript must be n.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:832","source_normalized_sha256":"6251c033ee2bb73a9591209a23e5b91d87f44de5fb6a3b741ff43783a39f947f","source_text":"j_1,\\ldots,j_r","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:842","target_normalized_sha256":"7af7ae41c45c803f2f0dc416dd876eb1c01539bfe378bcbc3e70a204e0fcf7a2","target_text":"j_1,\\ldots,j_n","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-distribution-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0336","math_ordinal":646,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proof declared nu_{X_1} as the distribution of X_1; mu_{X_1} is not defined in this section.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:926","source_normalized_sha256":"0a7062052b3cc2a07474482a2e1fb52286b66a9e86b9f476cb046643a6b6e385","source_text":"\\int(x+a)^2\\mu_{X_1}(dx)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:940","target_normalized_sha256":"1c4b058b5522072427f9178bfe80c657f71b6c38109a1d4473fc8a8fe79c5d50","target_text":"\\int(x+a)^2\\nu_{X_1}(dx)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-function-subscript","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0337","math_ordinal":738,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The Taylor argument defines the function h in the immediately preceding sentence; no h_i function is declared there.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:1092","source_normalized_sha256":"1eafbe8ad6f502ba8401f05dc6022f5cc31301dcc9b15690c8967a0bd2c3b724","source_text":"h_i''(t)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:1111","target_normalized_sha256":"930dcf593b652e6714001f170cc9203328abc8474806c87ef001fc8e38759212","target_text":"h''(t)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0338","math_ordinal":741,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The subsequent factorization subtracts b a_i and b c for every i. The printed expression leaves i free outside the sum and subtracts c only once syntactically.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:1104-1107","source_normalized_sha256":"742ec4752cdd19090d8bc4cdfacb6aff0ad2b78bdf1a767c0773233513f9f709","source_text":"\\Expn(\\exp(b\\sum_{i=0}^nX_i-a_i-c))","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:1122-1126","target_normalized_sha256":"0890fe0a2235a2fe85b8a1fc009f9cc09611b37a27b511f4a52e24594f7e2d79","target_text":"\\Expn(\\exp(b\\sum_{i=0}^n(X_i-a_i-c)))","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-zero-index-wald-off-by-one","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0339","math_ordinal":813,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Here Z sums X_n inclusively from n=0 through Y, so E(Z)=gamma sum_{n>=0}P(Y>=n)=gamma(E(Y)+1). The unshifted Wald form applies to a one-indexed or exclusive convention.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:1192","source_normalized_sha256":"5124fd6552129c68e4c5e18bed1a7936bdf1be230dd0136a23b7c890659f7bee","source_text":"\\Expn(Z)=\\gamma\\Expn(Y)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:1213","target_normalized_sha256":"85da7cd33706689e120ebf9993a1ae16a138fe48a02f7fb2f648ceaf137aee73","target_text":"\\Expn(Z)=\\gamma(\\Expn(Y)+1)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-factor","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0340","math_ordinal":964,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The endnote summarizes the Taylor estimate proved above, whose linear term is b a_i; omitting b contradicts both h'(0)=a_i and the preceding displayed bound.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt272.tex:1388","source_normalized_sha256":"98068e7d55bb6375e746750500649ad1d1b50c15e6fa28673b30ae00b647573c","source_text":"\\exp(a_i+\\bover18b^2)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt272.tex:1417","target_normalized_sha256":"4e8001087d0b13af6490b45339ca5fb402dea9a8e5e84a65785b89b1279c96d5","target_text":"\\exp(ba_i+\\bover18b^2)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S272"}
